>1</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fees-payments-and-payouts-pay-an-invoice-now" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Pay an invoice now</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open Invoices, then the invoice. It lists what it covers and the balance.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose Card (paid at once) and press <b class="gd-ui">Pay $...</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Or choose Pre-authorized debit (from a Canadian bank account, clears in 3 to 5 business days) and press <b class="gd-ui">Authorize debit of $...</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Prefer Interac e-Transfer? Send the amount to billing@carmacars.ca with the invoice number in the message.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/owner/invoices/INV-1050</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/742"><img src="/guides/img/owner-06-invoice-desktop-bba2c020.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="742"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:6.9%;top:52.6%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:38.2%;top:52.6%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:11.5%;top:80.5%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Paid us by e-Transfer, cheque, cash or bank transfer? Once we record it, the invoice says &quot;Paid by e-Transfer on&quot; the date, you get a receipt by email, and the automatic debit does not take that amount. Paid part of it? The invoice shows Partly paid and only the rest is debited.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fees-payments-and-payouts-tell-us-where-to-pay-you" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Tell us where to pay you</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Account</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Banking</b>. Under Where we pay you, choose Bank transfer or e-Transfer.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Fill in Account holder, Institution number, Transit number and Account number (or your e-Transfer email).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Submit payout details</b>. For your security we confirm new details by phone before we use them.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/owner/banking</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:990/642"><img src="/guides/img/owner-07-banking-desktop-87b2ffe3.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="990" height="642"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:50.5%;top:25.7%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:90.9%;top:45.5%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:30.3%;top:89.7%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fees-payments-and-payouts-statements-and-payouts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Statements and payouts</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">This month so far, at the top of Statements: the rentals finished this month, your Owner Revenue, the Revenue Share, fees and deductions and the expected payout, worked out live and marked Provisional. Rentals still under way are listed below it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Statements: one a month, once approved by CarmaCars; the approved statement is the final one. Open one to see every booking, the revenue share, deductions and the payout.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Download PDF</b> to keep a copy. We also email it to you with the PDF attached.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Payouts shows what was paid to you and when. Payouts are made on the 10th for the month before.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/owner/statements/380cc1bb-bfd5-4e55-8022-93a3b998ca74</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/792"><img src="/guides/img/owner-09-statement-desktop-fc5f9ea5.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="792"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:16%;top:30.6%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:66%;top:40.9%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Paid a flat monthly payment for a car? Its statement shows a Flat monthly payment line for the month (a part month by the day) instead of the Revenue Share. The car&#39;s rentals are listed without amounts paid to you, as CarmaCars keeps them, and there is no insurance or tracker fee for it. A booking expense is taken off only when we charge it to you; it then shows as an owner cost with its reason. Vehicles shows the amount and since when.</div></aside><h3 class="gd-h3">Fees taken from your statement</h3><p class="gd-p">If you agreed with CarmaCars to have your fees taken from your revenue statement, your invoices are not debited from your bank account. Each invoice is paid from your next owner statement (the line &quot;Invoice INV-..., paid from statement&quot;) and reads <b class="gd-ui">Paid from statement</b>. If a statement does not cover it, the rest is taken from the next one; an invoice still owing 2 months after its billing date is debited from your bank account after the usual notice.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">A flat monthly payment and your agreement</h3><p class="gd-p">If your cars are paid a flat monthly amount, your Enrollment Agreement is the <b class="gd-ui">Flat-Rate Vehicle Enrollment Agreement</b>: a fixed Monthly Amount per car on the payout date, part months by the day, no revenue share and no insurance or tracker fee. When your pay changes from one way to the other, Home shows <b class="gd-ui">Check and sign</b> for the new agreement.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fees-payments-and-payouts-repairs-and-partner-credits" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Repairs and partner credits</h2><p class="gd-p">If CarmaCars turns it on for you, <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Statements</b> also shows the repair costs and partner credits on your own cars this year, with who paid each repair. It is not part of your statements or payouts.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('owner', 'documents-and-forms', 'chapter', 'fees-payments-and-payouts', 'Your signed agreements, uploads and government forms are under Documents. Some forms are filled for you; Forms C and D are signed on screen with your witnesses beside you.

## Sign everything at once

Everything you sign on screen is in one place: Home shows how many are signed ("2 of 5 signed") and opens it with Check and sign.

1. Press **Check and sign** on Home (or open `carmacars.ca/owner/sign`). The list at the top shows each document: signed, in this package, or done elsewhere (Forms C and D, the bank debit).
2. Check the key values: your name, address, each car with its VIN and plate, your fees and Revenue Share. Something wrong? Press **Fix** next to it, change it, and come back.
3. Open any document to read it word for word: the agreements, the schedules and Forms A and B. The official registry forms are not in it: they are printed and signed in ink.
4. A code is optional: press **Verify by code** if you want the certificate to say a 6-digit code to your phone or email confirmed it was you (it is asked first only if CarmaCars turns it on).
5. Tick that you read the documents, draw your initials in the box beside each confirmation the Enrollment Agreement asks for, and tick the two consents (to sign electronically, to get your records electronically).
6. Draw your signature in the box with your finger, a pen or the mouse, then press **Sign all**. One signature is applied to each document; CarmaCars countersigns at the same moment and every signed copy is in Documents.
7. Each signed copy ends with a certificate of completion: when and where each step was done, and whether a code confirmed it was you. Anyone holding a copy can check it at carmacars.ca/verify.

## Read your agreements before approval

You can read both agreements as soon as you apply, before we approve your terms.

1. Press **Read your agreements** on Home (Documents and each car''s Onboarding checklist link to it too).
2. Each document is filled in from your application: your name, address and cars. It is marked "Terms pending approval": the fees, the Revenue Share and the agreement numbers read Pending approval until we set them.
3. Something wrong? Press **Fix** next to it. The Sign button stays off until we approve your terms; then Home shows **Check and sign** and we email you.

> Two owners: A car with a second owner on its ownership? Each owner named in the Title Schedule signs. The other owner gets their own link by email and signs the same documents on their phone or computer, the same way: the documents read, the confirmations initialled, the consents and their drawn signature (a code to their email only if they choose it or CarmaCars turns it on). The agreements take effect when the last owner signs; CarmaCars countersigns then.

> Good to know: Cannot draw a signature (for example with a disability)? Call us: an Admin can let you type your name instead.

> Good to know: Form A (the trust declaration) is for cars under the Co-Registrant or Transfer method; Form B (the lease summary) for cars under a Lease method. No witness is needed: they are in the same package. You can also sign one on its own page from Documents.

> Good to know: Every agreement is signed on screen, with the e-signature. A copy signed on paper is not accepted (a document you signed on paper before November 2026 stays on file as Signed on paper).

## We set up your car for you

When our team enters your car for you, you get one email: review the details and sign.

1. No sign-in yet? The email has a link to choose your password. It works once, for 24 hours; after that use Forgot password on the sign-in page.
2. Open `carmacars.ca/owner/review` (Home has **Review or correct your details**). Check your phone and address, and each car: plate, colour, odometer, your insurer and your lender. The terms we agreed are shown too.
3. Something wrong? Correct it and press **Save corrections**. Your documents are filled in again and we are told. A term you did not agree to: message us before you sign.
4. Everything right? Press **Everything is right: sign** and sign once.

## Sign an updated Vehicle Schedule

When we agree new terms for a car you already signed for, you sign an updated Vehicle Schedule. Home shows it first.

1. Open it from Home or the email. It shows what changes (now and updated) and the date it applies from.
2. Read the text, then sign the same way as your agreements: tick that you read it, initial the updated terms, tick the two consents, draw your signature and press **Sign** (a code to your phone or email is optional).
3. Your current terms stay until you sign. After that, your invoices and statements use the new ones from the date. The signed copy, with its certificate of completion, is in Documents.

## Form C on screen, with your witness beside you

Form C is the lender or lessor permission for a financed or leased car. It needs one witness, and you can sign it on screen when your witness is with you.

1. Open Documents. Under Forms to sign with witnesses, press **Sign Form C on screen**.
2. Tick that you read the form (a code to your phone or email is optional, unless CarmaCars turns it on).
3. Draw your initials beside each of the three acknowledgments, tick the two consents and draw your signature.
4. Hand the device to your witness, another adult. They type their full name and tick the statement "I witnessed (your name) sign in my presence." Press **Sign Form C**.

![](/guides/img/owner-16-form-c-screen-desktop-faa92983.jpg "desktop; size: 790 980; address: carmacars.ca/owner/documents/form-c/4898eb96-0cce-4efc-9fdd-740b4b4e9ad3; pins: 2 5.7 13.6, 3 32.9 55.1, 4 6.3 82.2")

## Form D on screen, with your two witnesses beside you

Form D is a limited power of attorney, once for all your cars. It needs two witnesses, and you sign it on screen with both of them beside you.

1. Open Documents. Under Forms to sign with witnesses, press **Sign Form D on screen**.
2. Tick that you read the form (a code to your phone or email is optional, unless CarmaCars turns it on), tick the two consents and draw your signature.
3. Hand the device to your first witness, another adult. They type their full name and tick the statement "I witnessed (your name) sign in my presence." Then the same for your second witness.
4. Press **Sign Form D**. CarmaCars signs Part 2 at the same moment, and the signed copy is in Documents.

> Good to know: A paper copy is no longer accepted: Forms C and D are signed on screen only. A form you sent as a photo before November 2026 stays on file.

## Government forms filled for you

Each car''s registry forms are filled in by themselves from your records as soon as its terms are approved, only the ones its onboarding method needs (013-1155 and 013-0169, for example, only for a Lease through a new corporation). When you add a missing value (your address, the odometer) they are filled in again by themselves. Until we load the official PDF, you get a data sheet with the values.

Open **Documents**: the **Government forms** box lists each one with its status and the date it was made.

1. Open Documents and choose a form marked "Official form, filled for you".
2. Press **Download the filled form** and check each value.
3. Print it and sign it in ink. It is the official ServiceOntario form exactly as ServiceOntario publishes it, with only its empty text boxes filled in. Its boxes to tick and its signatures are done by hand, at the registry office or before you go, as we tell you.

![](/guides/img/owner-13-official-form-desktop-48614913.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 732; address: carmacars.ca/owner/documents/forms/4d54a524-c28d-4bc4-8ad3-dd9558100a81/official; pins: 2 22.2 29.5")

> Good to know: ON00453 (a company''s registrant number) is an Adobe form: open it in Adobe Acrobat Reader (free) to see and print it. Other PDF viewers show a blank page, as they do with the form downloaded from ServiceOntario.

> Watch out: Official registry forms are never signed on screen. You pay ServiceOntario, the inspection station and the appraiser directly.

## The agreement for your deal

Your agreement is filled in from the terms we agreed with you. We email you a link when it is ready: **Read and sign** opens it in your portal, and you sign once for every document.

1. **Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement**: if your corporation leases cars to CarmaCars. It lists each car with its tier (Regular or Troubled), its monthly lease and its delivery date. Each car''s tier is set once, when it is delivered. You pay CarmaCars no fees. We pay in arrears on the 10th: a car''s first payment comes one full month after delivery, and part months are paid by the day, with the calculation on your statement.
2. **Referral Override Agreement**: if you referred another owner. It sets the override we pay you on their cars (out of our share, never theirs) and what you can see of those cars. Find it under **Cars**: Sign your Referral Override Agreement.
3. Something wrong in it? Reply to the email before you sign and we fix it.
